# .agentignore — personal-context blocklist for framework/
#
# Lives at: personal/.agentignore
# Read by:  framework/agent/scripts/check-context.sh (called from pre-commit)
#
# SYNTAX (gitignore-aligned):
#
#   foo/                  → PATH pattern. Files under this path are EXEMPT
#                            from scanning. Use for real infrastructure refs
#                            (vendor dirs, font names in code, MCP tool IDs).
#
#   !word                 → WORD pattern. If this string appears in any
#                            non-exempt framework/ file, the commit is
#                            BLOCKED. Case-insensitive substring match.
#
#   # comment             → ignored
#
#   <blank>               → ignored
#
# Inline override (on the content line, not in this file):
#   <content> # context-allow:<reason>
#                         → that one line is skipped from the scan.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXEMPT PATHS — files in these paths are not scanned
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Vendor infrastructure (MCP server collection — genuinely vendor-coupled)
framework/mcp/servers/

# Pptx skill — legitimate references to brand fonts ("Clean") in code
framework/skills/pptx/

# Vendor dirs and lockfiles never need scanning
node_modules/
package-lock.json
package.json

# Binary assets
SCREENSHOT.jpg

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLAG WORDS — these MUST NOT appear in non-exempt framework/ files
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your personal identifiers
# !<your-first-name>
# !<your-username>
# !@<your-username>

# Customer names (add as engagements happen — the `agentignore` skill
# can help curate this list)
# !<customer-name>
# !<contact-first-name> <contact-last-name>

# Internal product codes / project codenames
# !<internal-product-code>
